 61CU    60NI(3HE,D)                   1990SE03,1981KI06,2013SC0615NDS    201503
 61CU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=KAZIMIERZ ZUBER, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 125, 1 (2015)$       
 61CU2 H CUT=25-Jan-2015$                                                       
 61CU c  2013Sc06, 2013ScZZ: E({+3}He)=18 MeV from WNSL-Yale tandem accelerator 
 61CU2c  facility. Measured deuteron spectra, |s(|q), spectroscopic             
 61CU3c  factor C{+2}S using a split-pole spectrograph. FWHM |?50 keV.          
 61CU4c  Target=204 |mg/cm{+2} thick, 99.7% enriched. Deduced levels, J, |p.    
 61CU5c  DWBA analysis. Comparison with shell-model calculations.               
 61CU c  The main purpose of the neutron adding and neutron removal reaction    
 61CU2c  studies by 2013Sc06 was to obtain occupancies of neutron orbitals,     
 61CU3c  proton vacancies, and energy centroids of neutron, neutron-holes,      
 61CU4c  proton-single particle excitations in {+60}Ni and {+62}Ni, and thereby 
 61CU5c  investigate closure of 0f{-7/2} shell. Some data details of this study 
 61CU6c  are supplied in 2013ScZZ                                               
 61CU c  1990Se03: E=33 MeV. Measured |s(|q), |q=12.5|'-115|' (lab.) in steps   
 61CU2c  of 2.5|', with six |DE-E telescopes, FWHM=55 keV. Target enriched to   
 61CU3c  98.5% of {+60}Ni. DWBA analysis.                                       
 61CU c  1981Ki06: E=18 MeV. Measured |s(|q), |q=1.6|'-40|'. Magnetic           
 61CU2c  spectrograph, FWHM=12-15 keV. Enriched target. J dependent effects at  
 61CU3c  small angles.                                                          
 61CU c  1976Br36: E=18 MeV. Measured |s(|q), |q(c.m.)=5|'-90|', magnetic       
 61CU2c  spectrograph, FWHM|?20 keV. Enriched target.                           
 61CU c  1968Pu03 (also 1966Ro13): E=16.4 MeV. Measured deuteron spectra,       
 61CU2c  |s(|q), DWBA analysis. Magnetic spectrometer FWHM=19 keV               
 61CU c  Others:                                                                
 61CU c  1979Fi02, 1976Bo06: E=30.2 MeV. Measured |s(|q) with |DE-E semi        
 61CU2c  telescope, FWHM|?50 keV. Data for seven analog states from 6450 to     
 61CU3c  9960 keV                                                               
 61CU c  1975Ba63: E=6.5, 7 MeV. Magnetic spectrometer. Data for g.s. and 470   
 61CU2c  level                                                                  
 61CU c  1965Bl05: data for four isobaric analog states, FWHM=70 keV            
 61CU c  L values and spectroscopic factors are from comparisons with DWBA      
 61CU2c  calculations with normalization factor =4.42 (1981Ki06).               
 61CU c  Most data are from 1990Se03, except as noted. There is good agreement  
 61CU2c  with the data of 1976Br36, if account is taken of the different DWBA   
 61CU3c  normalization constant (N=3.2 from sum-rule limits) used in 1976Br36   
 61CU4c  and (N=4.42) in 1990Se03.                                              
 61CU c  All data of E|<3578 are from Adopted Levels rounded to nearest keV     
 61CU2c  (1981Ki06). All data with E>3578 are from 1990Se03, except as noted.   
 61CU c  Cross sections listed under comments are from 1968Pu03 corresponding   
 61CU2c  to the value at first maximum in |s(|q) pattern                        
